  "body": "10A - Sold\r\n10B - Sold\r\n10C - Sold\r\n10D - Sold\r\n10E - AVAILABLE\r\n\r\nWith striking architectural lines, dark and white exterior accents, and a clean, symmetrical facade, they create a bold yet elegant street presence. Floor-to-ceiling windows and glass balconies flood the interiors with natural light and give a boutique, urban edge that blends effortlessly into this premium development.\r\n\r\nOffers an inviting open-plan kitchen, dining, and living area, perfectly positioned to capture natural light from its north-facing, fully fenced deck. Two sliding doors create seamless flow to the outdoors, making entertaining easy. A guest toilet is also conveniently located on the ground floor. Upstairs, you'll find three double bedrooms including a master suite with walk-in wardrobe and private ensuite, plus an internal access garage for added security and ease.\r\n\r\n\r\n-Spacious living/dining area opens to balcony and backyard\r\n-Kitchen with breakfast bar for casual meals\r\n-Two ranch sliders connect to a private, fenced deck\r\n-3 upstairs bedrooms including a master with ensuite\r\n-Internal access garage\r\n\r\nFeatures a clever layout with a study nook and guest toilet on the ground level, along with internal garage access. The first floor hosts a generous open-plan living and dining space that opens to a sunny balcony at the front and a private backyard off the kitchen - perfect for indoor-outdoor flow. A stylish breakfast bar adds everyday convenience. Upstairs includes three well-sized bedrooms, with the master bedroom enjoying its own ensuite for extra comfort, and sea view. \r\n\r\nJust a few minutes' walk to Half Moon Bay shops, cafés, the supermarket, and the ferry terminal, making your city commute a breeze. Plus, the bus stop is literally just steps from your door. Zoned for top schools: Pigeon Mountain Primary and Farm Cove intermediate",
